{"commit": "5b512dce33d186f4fbe7ed3fa7a5dc7e33d73823", "id": "5b512dce33d186f4fbe7ed3fa7a5dc7e33d73823-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Reversal changes are not part of the upstream fix", "repo": "https://github.com/rapidfuzz/strsim-rs", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260923T150237Z-3ea669d8", "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "strsim", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Fix transposition counting in Jaro / JaroWinkler (#56)", "summary": "The original transposition counter walked `a` left-to-right and tracked the most-recently-matched `b`-position in `b_match_index`; whenever a new match landed at a smaller `j`, it incremented `transpositions`. This is not the textbook Jaro algorithm and produces asymmetric results: `jaro(\"a jke\", \"jane a k\") = 0.683` but `jaro(\"jane a k\", \"a jke\") = 0.6`. The fix replaces the counter with the correct two-pass walk over the matched-flag arrays, dividing the count by 2.", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T15:02:37.630650+00:00"}
