ndercounts reordered matches and can produce asymmetric similarity scores: the added regression assertion expects approximately 0.6 for jaro(\"a jke\", \"jane a k\"), whereas the old counter yields approximately 0.683. The fix records matched positions in both sequences, compares their matched elements in order, and halves the mismatch count. The reversal restores the original matching and scoring region while preserving the fixed search-range handling and all upstream tests. Both source regions occur exactly once in their respective revisions. No tests were run.", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T15:19:23.063330+00:00"}
